 </details>
 <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #e8e4dc;padding:1rem 0;">
  <summary style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);cursor:pointer;font-size:1.02rem;">How far is the Quarry Exhibit Hall from Jensen?</summary>
  <p style="margin-top:.7rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;">The Quarry Visitor Center is 7 miles north of Jensen off Utah State Highway 149.<sup>1</sup> From Vernal the total drive is roughly 20 miles.</p>
 </details>
 <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #e8e4dc;padding:1rem 0;">
  <summary style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);cursor:pointer;font-size:1.02rem;">Does Jensen have fuel, groceries or restaurants?</summary>
  <p style="margin-top:.7rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;">Not reliably, and nothing you should plan around. Treat Vernal, 13 miles west on US-40, as the last full services before the monument.</p>
 </details>
 <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #e8e4dc;padding:1rem 0;">
  <summary style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);cursor:pointer;font-size:1.02rem;">Is Jensen the right turning for the dinosaur bones?</summary>
  <p style="margin-top:.7rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;">Yes, for the Utah side. Utah State Highway 149 leaves US-40 at Jensen and runs 7 miles north to the Quarry Visitor Center.<sup>1</sup> The Canyon Visitor Center on the Colorado side has canyon and river scenery but no quarry.<sup>1</sup></p>
 </details>
 <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #e8e4dc;padding:1rem 0;">
  <summary style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);cursor:pointer;font-size:1.02rem;">What does it cost to enter the monument, and how do you reach the Exhibit Hall?</summary>
  <p style="margin-top:.7rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;">Both are set by the National Park Service and are covered on our <a href="/hotel-near-dinosaur-national-monument" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:700;">Dinosaur National Monument guide</a>, including the seasonal shuttle. Nothing is sold in Jensen — arrive with a pass or the means to buy one.</p>
 </details>
 <details style="border-bottom:1px solid #e8e4dc;padding:1rem 0;">
  <summary style="font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);cursor:pointer;font-size:1.02rem;">Should I stay in Jensen or Vernal?</summary>
  <p style="margin-top:.7rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;font-weight:300;">Vernal — Jensen has no lodging at all. Vernal is 13 miles west on US-40 and is the nearest town with hotels, groceries, fuel and restaurants.</p>
 </details>
</div>

<div class="content-section" style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);">
 <h2 style="font-size:1.1rem;">Sources</h2>
 <ol style="line-height:1.9;padding-left:1.2rem;">
  <li>Dinosaur National Monument, National Park Service — two visitor centers and their states, Quarry Visitor Center location 7 miles north of Jensen via Utah State Highway 149, seasonal shuttle versus private vehicle access, monument address and telephone. <a href="https://www.nps.gov/dino/index.htm" rel="noopener nofollow" style="color:var(--navy);">nps.gov/dino</a></li>
 </ol>
 <p style="margin-top:.8rem;">Fees, hours and shuttle operation for the monument are set by the National Park Service and change. Confirm before travelling. Last reviewed ${BUSINESS.lastUpdated}.</p>
</div>

